  "notes": "\"CTH\" in label matrix and \"T\" and \"CTH\" etched in runouts denote [l=Columbia Records Pressing Plant, Terre Haute], pressing.\n\nTML stamped in runouts - The letter after the dash indicates which lathe was used (M = Master, S = Slave).\n\nLabel variant to another Terre Haute pressing [r=4438327], with 15 Columbus Circle address and no Warner lozenge logo in rimtext.\n\nOn labels:\nAll Songs Published By Benchmark Music ASCAP\n℗ 1974 Asylum Records\nAsylum Records Mfg. by Elektra/Asylum/Nonesuch Records. A Division of Warner Communications Inc., 15 Columbus Circle, New York, N.Y. 10023\n\nOn jacket:\n℗ © 1974 Elektra/Asylum/Nonesuch Records - 15 Columbus Circle, N.Y., N.Y. 10023 - A Division Of Warner Communications Inc. - Printed in U.S.A.\n\nRecorded at Elektra Sound Recorders, Sunset Sound and at Hollywood Sound Recorders. Mixed at Hollywood Sound Recorders.\n\nLyrics available on request from Warner Brothers Publications.\n\nCover concept: if it's all reet with Magritte\n\nFor Phyllis and Ethan c/s\n",
  "released_formatted": "13 Sep 1974",
